    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "**SwiftUI** — native platform play, best UX/performance for iOS. Only bet React Native if you need Android parity too.\n\n**launchd** — it's the macOS-native answer. PM2 works if the bridge is Node-based, but launchd is built for exactly this (persistent services, system integration). Platform-native beats generic process managers.\n\n**Queue offline messages** — worth the complexity. Phone apps hit spotty networks constantly; users expect the app to absorb the hiccup. Fire-and-forget failures feel broken.\n\n**Tailscale is fine** — solid for internal/dev access. Just clarify: if this is for customer-facing remote features, you'll want formal infrastructure instead. But if it's your team accessing the bridge, Tailscale is clean and low-ops.\n\n↳ thread: which of these is closest to uncertain for your use case?"
    }
   ],
